592186064388 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317512 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186068866 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317331 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186069273 1068 #edb/ref 17592186066778 13194139533418 17592186045585 false] [17592186069273 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316834 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186069273 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186069273 1071 "The equation $x^{2} + 8x - 33 = 0$ can be written in the form $(x + p)^{2} = q$. Find $p + q$, and solve the equation." 13194139533418 17592186045585 false] [17592186069273 1071 "The equation ${x}^{2}+8x-33=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,p+q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186069273 1074 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x-33 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =33 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2})-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16 & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=49,$ and $p+q=53.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4+7=3 \\\\ x & =-4-7=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-11$ and $x=3.$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186078391 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317412 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186078391 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317413 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186078391 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317414 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186078391 1038 #edb/ref 1759218631