ed}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{2}{{2}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120309 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117963 13194139533418 17592186045585 false] [17592186120309 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316919 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120309 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120309 1071 "The vectors $a_{1}$, $a_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b ∈ Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$ from the decomposition $b = x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2}$.\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 false] [17592186120309 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120309 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-2)=-6.$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120312 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117981 13194139533418 17592186045585 false] [17592186120312 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316791 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120312 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186120312 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π: r = sb + tc$, $t, s ∈ R$, where $b = ⟨ - 1, 3, 5⟩$, $c = ⟨1,-5,-7⟩$, and