aligned}4({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (4{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +2\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (4{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form ${x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$ for some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ 2(2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficients of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166873 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317223 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166873 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317224 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166873 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317249 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166873 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317250 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317398 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317399 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317400 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317401 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317402 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166966 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317403 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186166967 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317405 13194139533418 175