B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2s+8=A(s+2)+B(s+3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-3)+8=A(-3+2)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,2=-1A\\,⟹\\,A=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(-2)+8=A(0)+B(-2+3)\\,⟹\\,4=1B\\,⟹\\,B=4.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{2}{s+3}+\\frac{4}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\ y(t) & =-2{e}^{-3t}+4{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316762 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1069 "q-342937" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1071 "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}$ at the point where $x=3.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1072 #uuid "9ce56e89-e4a0-55d3-bc60-994f61368da9" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317347 1074 "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-4x+(-2(x-2{)}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-4x-\\frac{2}{(x-2{)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =-4(3)-\\frac{2}{(3-2{)}^{3}} \\\\  & =-12-2 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=3$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(3)=-14.\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317348 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316884 1319413953341