385 1072 #uuid "706637d8-3249-598f-a5d8-c8392fda6792" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317385 1074 "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-2W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-2W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-2\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-2x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-2x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{-2\\cdot 0} \\\\ 5 & =C \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=5{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(3) & =5{e}^{-2\\cdot 3}=5{e}^{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316926 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1069 "q-34327" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1071 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0}$\n- $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=2y}$\n- $C={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1072 #uuid "92efc5e4-6fcf-5867-b774-9cceef4cda9c" 13194139533418 17592186045585 true] [17592186317386 1074 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. It actually represents the whole space ${R}^{2}$, since the coordinates of any vector $⟨x,y⟩$ satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if 